# QA Automation Pipeline — Guardrails

## Existing agents (read-only)

Never modify: `.cursor/agents/test-planner|test-generator|test-healer|headed-executor|headless-executor.agent.md` or `.github/agents/playwright-test-*.agent.md`.

Only new agent allowed for this workflow: `qa-automation-pipeline`.

Orchestrate; do not duplicate generator/healer logic or merge into those agents.

## Security

- No hard-coded credentials/PII/transaction data; mask secrets in logs/reports
- Use `.env` / fixtures; synthetic/approved data only
- No destructive production runs; confirm non-prod before MCP execution

## Pipeline quality

- No fabricated requirements, locators, APIs, expected results, or execution results
- Invalid Excel rows never reach generation
- Claim execution only with evidence; otherwise `Blocked` + reason
- Reuse Playwright POM/fixtures/helpers; no second framework
- Healing: minimal evidence-based fixes; never weaken assertions to force pass
- Do not modify application source to make tests pass unless explicitly authorized

## Edits

Before writes: list paths + why; avoid protected agents and unrelated app sources; record file summary under `results/qa-pipeline/final/`.
